  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the force is given by $\\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{at}+\\mathrm{bt}^{2}$ with $\\mathrm{t}$ as time. The dimensions of a and b are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4wgfD",
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{MLT}^{-4}\\right]$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{MLT}^{-2}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "t4V69",
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{MLT}^{-3}\\right]$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{MLT}^{-4}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Z19xB",
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{2} \\mathrm{~T}^{-3}\\right]$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{2} \\mathrm{~T}^{-2}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XqNCv",
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{2} \\mathrm{~T}^{-3}\\right]$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{3} \\mathrm{~T}^{-4}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Dimension of at = Dimension of F \r\n$[a t]=[F] \\Rightarrow[a]=\\left[\\frac{F}{t}\\right]$\r\n$[b]=\\left[\\frac{M L T^{-2}}{T}\\right] \\Rightarrow[a]=\\left[M L T^{-3}\\right]$\r\nDimension of $\\mathrm{bt}^{2}=$ Dimension of $\\mathrm{F}$\r\n$\\left[\\mathrm{bt}^{2}\\right]=[\\mathrm{F}] \\Rightarrow[\\mathrm{b}]=\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{F}}{\\mathrm{t}^{2}}\\right]$\r\n$[\\mathrm{b}]=\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{ML} \\mathrm{T}^{-4}}{\\mathrm{~T}^{2}}\\right] \\Rightarrow[\\mathrm{b}]=\\left[\\mathrm{MLT}^{-4}\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
